Vikram and Betal: The Honest Choice (Raw Story)

King Vikram was carrying Betal through a dark forest.

As always, Betal told him a story.

“Listen carefully, Vikram,” said Betal. “Once there was a kind boy who found a purse full of gold coins on the road.”

The boy picked it up and thought, “This must belong to someone.”

Soon, a rich man came looking for his lost purse.

The boy returned it and said, “Here is your purse, sir.”

The rich man checked it and said, “Some coins are missing! You must have taken them!”

The boy was shocked. “I did not take anything!”

The case was taken to the king.

The king thought for a while and said, “This purse does not belong to the rich man.”

Everyone was surprised.

The king explained, “The boy said he found a purse full of coins, but the rich man claims some are missing. So this must not be his purse.”

The boy was rewarded for his honesty.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, who was right?”

Vikram replied, “The king was right because he trusted honesty over greed.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Honesty is always rewarded.
